# Table

Rows and columns for structured, comparable records. Basecoat styles a
semantic `<table>` from the single `table` class; everything else —
caption, header, footer, cell alignment — is the platform's table
markup.

<%= embed :table, :default %>

```html
<div class="overflow-x-auto">
  <table class="table">
    <caption>A list of your recent invoices.</caption>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Invoice</th>
        <th>Status</th>
        <th class="text-right">Amount</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td class="font-medium">INV001</td>
        <td>Paid</td>
        <td class="text-right">$250.00</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
    <tfoot>
      <tr>
        <td colspan="2">Total</td>
        <td class="text-right">$2,500.00</td>
      </tr>
    </tfoot>
  </table>
</div>
```

## When to use

- Collections where users compare fields across records: referral
  lists, episode histories, audit trails.
- Anything users scan by column (who, when, status).

## When not to use

- A handful of heterogeneous records where each is read alone —
  cards in a grid read better than a 3-row table.
- Key-value pairs of a single record — a definition-style layout in
  a `card`, not a two-column table.
- Layout — never use a table to position things.

## Anatomy and options

A semantic `<table class="table">` inside basecoat's documented
`overflow-x-auto` wrapper. The markup is the API:

- `caption` names the collection; `thead`/`tbody`/`tfoot` as usual.
- Cells take any content — links, `badge` spans, buttons — and any
  utility: `text-right tabular-nums` for numerics, `font-medium` for
  identity columns, `<th scope="row">` for row headers.
- For long scrolling tables, pin the header with
  `<thead class="sticky top-0 z-10 bg-background">`.

Long collections paginate via `pagination` — the table renders the
current page only.

## Do and don't

- Do order columns by scan priority: identity first, then status,
  then detail; timestamps usually last.
- Do right-align numeric columns and use `tabular-nums`.
- Do render an empty collection as the table's empty state copy
  ("No contacts match the selected date range."), not a bare header
  row.
- Don't let one verbose column destroy row scanning — truncate
  detail text and let the row link carry users to it.
- Don't put state colour on whole rows; a `badge` in a status cell
  marks state without painting the table.

## Accessibility and content

- Real `<table>`/`<thead>`/`<th>` semantics — column association is
  announced; the sticky header is CSS only.
- Use `<caption>` to name the collection when the table isn't
  directly under a heading.
- Header labels are short nouns, sentence case, no units in cells
  that the header can carry ("Wait (days)").
